      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi alloy has favorable plasticity and machinability.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNiTi alloy has relatively low hardness and strength.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is addition of 0.5–1.0 at.% interstitial carbon to CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "intervention; falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 0.5–1.0 at.% carbon addition can be introduced while retaining a single-phase FCC solid solution and avoiding brittle intermetallic phases.",
      "field": "intervention; conditions; falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon increases local lattice distortion.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon induces or optimizes short-range order in FCC CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-induced lattice distortion strengthens the alloy through stronger interactions with dislocations.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Short-range order raises the resistance and energy barrier experienced by leading partial dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9645729::web::010::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation passage through an SRO-containing FCC matrix creates diffuse antiphase boundaries that exert back stress and retard dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9645729::web::010::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The combined lattice-distortion and SRO effects enhance solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body",
        "PMC9645729::web::010::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped CoCrFeNiTi will have measurably and statistically significantly higher hardness than undoped CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome; falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body",
        "PMC5227964::web::011::deformation_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped CoCrFeNiTi will have measurably and statistically significantly higher compressive strength than undoped CoCrFeNiTi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome; falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body",
        "PMC5227964::web::011::deformation_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped CoCrFeNiTi will retain its good compressive plasticity or show only a modest reduction in ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::002::body",
        "PMC5227964::web::011::deformation_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed strengthening and ductility balance applies from room temperature through 600 °C under compressive loading.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excess carbon could lead to carbide precipitation.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::web::011::deformation_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
